Runtime text editor subpixel spacing threshold validation - 2026-07-03

Source change:
- zircon_editor/src/ui/retained_host/host_contract/paint_text/draw/layout.rs
- Kept the retained-host text bridge on runtime-provided displayed text and line width.
- Tightened per-grapheme runtime advance acceptance from a loose max(1.25px, host * 25%) window to clamp(host * 6%, 0.35px, 0.60px).
- Added named constants for total-run and per-grapheme tolerances, avoiding new inline magic thresholds.
- Added regression: runtime_positioned_glyphs_rejects_subpixel_tab_label_jitter.
- Regression string: "editor base.zui", matching the editor tab label family of the user-provided screenshot.
- Regression intent: a +0.75px / -0.75px local advance shift keeps total width close but is visible at editor tab size, so retained-host drawing falls back to the selected host face's natural glyph spacing.

